# Example override file for replacing package versions (e.g. PyTorch builds
# for GPUs the default build does not support).
#
# How it works: this file is passed to uv via the UV_OVERRIDE environment
# variable. Every version pin here OVERRIDES the corresponding pin in
# requirements.txt during resolution — packages are installed once, with
# no reinstall churn on container restarts.
#
# Usage:
#   1. Copy this file into your data volume, e.g.:
#        cp user_requirements.txt.example <your_data_dir>/user_requirements.txt
#   2. Set the environment variables (path is INSIDE the container):
#        UV_OVERRIDE=/data/user_requirements.txt
#        UV_EXTRA_INDEX_URL=https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu126
#      (pick the index that matches the CUDA build you need)
#   3. Uncomment ONE of the sections below and restart the container.
#
# For GTX 10xx (Pascal, sm_61): PyTorch dropped Pascal in CUDA 12.8+ builds.
# CUDA 12.6 builds are the last ones that still include it:
# torch==2.7.1+cu126
# torchvision==0.22.1+cu126
# torchaudio==2.7.1+cu126
#
# For RTX 50xx (Blackwell, sm_120): requires CUDA 12.8+ builds
# (UV_EXTRA_INDEX_URL=https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu128):
# torch==2.8.0+cu128
# torchvision==0.23.0+cu128
# torchaudio==2.8.0+cu128
#
# For CPU-only installation
# (UV_EXTRA_INDEX_URL=https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu):
# torch==2.8.0+cpu
# torchvision==0.23.0+cpu
# torchaudio==2.8.0+cpu
